From ec8c2299f24d3e7129391365330d58e26b19f1d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:56:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): backup integration race condition on Windows CI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: uniq() used SystemTime::now() which on Windows has ~15ms
resolution (GetSystemTimeAsFileTime). Two parallel backup tests calling
config_con_backup_en_temp() within the same ~15ms window got the same
uniq() value, shared the same tmp/backup_int_<X> directory, and the
faster test's LimpiarTemporal::drop deleted the shared dir while the
slower (encrypted) test was still reading its backup file →
Os { code: 3, kind: NotFound, PATH_NOT_FOUND }.

This explains why only restauracion_de_backup_cifrado_con_gbak_real
failed: the encryption path (cifrar_archivo + remove temporal) is
slower than the plain gbak path, so it was still running when the
non-encrypted test finished and cleaned up the shared tmp dir.

Fix:
1. Add a process-wide AtomicU64 counter to uniq() so every call
   returns a distinct value regardless of clock resolution.
2. Mark all 4 backup tests #[serial_test::serial] as defense-in-depth
   to also prevent gbak.exe / Firebird Embedded engine contention
   when 4 tests spawn gbak subprocesses simultaneously. The crate
   is already in dev-dependencies (serial_test = "3").

Verified: the 4 tests now have isolated, guaranteed-unique tmp dirs
and run sequentially.
